A||N||8||burdell1||Car won't start....||||1||
Z||000000||burdell1||07-06-2000||02:58 PM||||After having some major problems with my Fiero (see link <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004397.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004397.html</A> <BR>I finally bought a different car....now, when I try to start the Fiero, it won't start. The battery is dead, so I have to jump start it...then when I try to start it I keep hearing a clicking noise....could it be the starter motor?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||lennyb4||07-06-2000||03:07 PM||||If your hearing a "clicking" noise, i'd bet ten to one that its your starter sileniod (yea i know i spelled it wrong, two hours left on a double shift).||||reg||6
Z||000002||burdell1||07-06-2000||03:21 PM||||is that expensive to replace?||||reg||1
Z||000003||ROB MAC||07-06-2000||03:30 PM||||solenoid is on the starter I believe<BR>not expensive but not a fun job.<BR>check connections to the starter and battery <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||lennyb4||07-06-2000||03:38 PM||||You can buy a replacement for around $15.00. You do how ever have to drop the starter to replace it. Its held on by two small bolts that thread into the top of the starter housing. Make sure you get a new spring with it (it should be included but ive bought them where they forgot to place it in the box). Its also a good time to clean and check all connections including grounds.||||reg||1
Z||000005||burdell1||07-15-2000||02:54 PM||||what do the wires look like between the starter and the battery?||||reg||1
Z||000006||286SE'S||07-17-2000||03:15 PM||||Both my brother and me have had the same problem with our Fieros. That click or nothing when the key was turned. Battery fine. Mine<BR>was intermittent and drove me nuts for two years. I finally replaced my starter because when I took it off to change the solonoid I found that the teeth on the gear was amost shot. Be prepared for that.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000007||burdell1||07-25-2000||02:01 PM||||Does anyone have a picture of where the starter would be on a V6?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||b lo 0||07-25-2000||03:37 PM||||Look on the transaxle in the area that the crankshaft enters the tranny. (I think it's the passenger side)  The starter drives the flexplate, which is in the area of the torque converter (or flywheel if manual).  You can't miss it, it's a cylinder about 8-10 inches long (motor) with a smaller cylinder (solenoid) attached to the side.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>GAWD I love this car||||reg||1
